1
00:00:00,338 --> 00:00:02,468
(Sheldon:)Scrimmage.

2
00:00:03,382 --> 00:00:06,512
(Sheldon:)The line of scrimmage
is the imaginary transverse line...

3
00:00:06,677 --> 00:00:09,177
...separating the offense
from the defense.

4
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:11,180
(Leonard:)Oh.

5
00:00:11,807 --> 00:00:14,057
(Howard:)Sheldon knows football?

6
00:00:14,644 --> 00:00:19,144
(Leonard:)-Apparently.
-I mean, Quidditch, sure. But football?

7
00:00:21,317 --> 00:00:24,447
(Leonard:)-Sheldon, how do you know this stuff?
-I grew up in Texas.

8
00:00:24,612 --> 00:00:26,652
(Sheldon:)Football is ubiquitous in Texas.

9
00:00:26,822 --> 00:00:30,742
There's pro football, college football,
high school football, peewee football....

10
00:00:30,910 --> 00:00:35,500
(Sheldon:)In fact, every form of football
except the original, European football.

11
00:00:35,665 --> 00:00:38,955
(Sheldon:)Which most Texans believe
to be a commie plot.

12
00:00:40,503 --> 00:00:42,003
(Leonard:)-Unbelievable.
-If interested...

13
00:00:42,171 --> 00:00:46,671
(Sheldon:)...I also know all about frying meat
that isn't chicken as if it were chicken.

14
00:00:50,012 --> 00:00:51,802
(Leonard:)So you could teach me?

15
00:00:52,723 --> 00:00:55,683
(Sheldon:)Football or chicken-fried meats?

16
00:00:56,602 --> 00:00:59,692
(Leonard:)Football. I'm going to Penny's
to watch a game with her friends.

